claim.claim-text:
an image acquiring unit that acquires a plurality of medical images including a first medical image and a second medical image preceding the first medical image in time series;
an emphasis processing unit that emphasizes a first region of interest and a second region of interest at a set emphasis degree, the first region of interest being included in the first medical image, the second region of interest being included in the second medical image;
a total-time measuring unit that measures a total time during which the first region of interest and the second region of interest are detected or emphasized;
an emphasis-degree setting unit that sets the emphasis degree to a relatively larger value as the total time is relatively longer; and
an identical-region-of-interest determining unit that determines whether the first region of interest is identical with the second region of interest,
wherein in a case in which the identical-region-of-interest determining unit determines that the first region of interest is identical with the second region of interest, the total-time measuring unit measures a total time of the first region of interest by taking over a total time of the second region of interest.

the image acquiring unit acquires a third medical image preceding the second medical image in time series;
the emphasis processing unit emphasizes a third region of interest included in the third medical image at a set emphasis degree;
the total-time measuring unit measures a total time during which the third region of interest is detected or emphasized;
in a case in which the identical-region-of-interest determining unit determines that the first region of interest is not identical with the second region of interest, the identical-region-of-interest determining unit further determines whether the first region of interest is identical with the third region of interest on the basis of a similarity degree between the first region of interest and the third region of interest; and
in a case in which the identical-region-of-interest determining unit determines that the first region of interest is identical with the third region of interest, the total-time measuring unit measures a total time of the first region of interest by taking over a total time of the third region of interest.

an image acquiring step for acquiring a plurality of medical images including a first medical image and a second medical image preceding the first medical image in time series;
an emphasis processing step for emphasizing a first region of interest and a second region of interest at a set emphasis degree, the first region of interest being included in the first medical image, the second region of interest being included in the second medical image;
a total-time measuring step for measuring a total time during which the first region of interest and the second region of interest are detected or emphasized;
an emphasis-degree setting step for setting the emphasis degree to a relatively larger value as the total time is relatively longer; and
an identical-region-of-interest determining step for determining whether the first region of interest is identical with the second region of interest,
wherein in a case in which the identical-region-of-interest determining step determines that the first region of interest is identical with the second region of interest, the total-time measuring step measures a total time of the first region of interest by taking over a total time of the second region of interest.
